= Automated market maker =

== Overview ==
'''Automated market maker''' is a rule-based market mechanism that quotes or executes trades algorithmically against on-chain or otherwise pooled liquidity rather than requiring each trade to match a contemporaneous opposing order.

In many DeFi AMMs, liquidity providers supply asset reserves to a pool and traders swap against those reserves. A pricing or invariant function determines how reserves and marginal prices change as trades occur.

AMM is a broad design family. Constant-product, stable-swap, weighted, concentrated-liquidity, and other mechanisms differ in invariants, capital efficiency, risk exposure, and price behavior.

Arbitrage commonly links AMM prices to external markets. This does not make the AMM itself an oracle of fundamental value; its observed price is produced by reserves, trades, fees, and arbitrage under market conditions.

== Boundaries ==
* AMM ≠ constant-product market maker only
* AMM ≠ liquidity pool by identity
* algorithmic quote ≠ externally correct price

